        <mxCell id="sL9hEpOnEqMbaMQWPS6v-76" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;spacing=0;" value="&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;animating&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0,0,0&quot;&gt;App VM requires only outbound HTTPS (port 443) to an internal Azure Private Endpoint, no direct public internet access.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0,1,0&quot;&gt;Azure OpenAI instance to be provisioned and managed under the client&#39;s existing enterprise Azure subscription.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0,2,0&quot;&gt;RHEL VM to Azure OpenAI connectivity must route securely via internal networks (e.g., VPN/ExpressRoute), avoiding the public internet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0,3,0&quot;&gt;Storage can be dynamically expanded in the future via hypervisor disk resizing and standard RHEL LVM.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
